SUMMARY:Drop-in Advising for Undergraduate Students
LOCATION:Center for Career Development
DESCRIPTION:Drop-ins are 20-minute\, advising sessions for undergraduates
  that do not require an appointment. In-person drop-ins for the fall sem
 ester begin on Monday\, August 31 and are held most weekdays from 2-4 p.
 m. Students are welcome to come at any point during those times that fit
  their schedules. They are held at the Center for Career Development (ab
 ove the U-Store on 36 University Place). You can come to drop-ins to jus
 t talk through your interests and possible options\, you do not need to 
 have anything prepared to meet with an adviser. Common topics covered du
 ring drop-in sessions include: - How the Center for Career Development c
 an help you - Starting to explore career options - Resume and cover lett
 er reviews - Preparing for career fairs - Job/internship/fellowship appl
 ication help - Networking strategies and how to contact alumni - Plannin
 g for summer experiences and reflection This progr\nRegister: https://pr
 inceton.joinhandshake.com/stu/events?collection=ALL&eventFormat=IN_PERSO
 N&sort=RELEVANCE&date=ALL&keyword=Drop-in%20Advising%20for%20Undergradua
 te%20Students\nhttps://careerdevelopment.princeton.edu/events/drop-advis
 ing-undergraduate-students-28
URL:https://careerdevelopment.princeton.edu/events/drop-advising-undergra
 duate-students-28
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
