SUMMARY:From Asia to Wall Street and Beyond: An Alum's Global Career Path
LOCATION:Center for Career Development
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a chat for students thinking about international 
 careers. Moderated by Molly Giblin\, the director of program for Princet
 on in Asia (PiA)\, this conversation with David Willard '06 will focus o
 n how he built his career in China and will provide practical advice for
  students weighing a year or more abroad after graduation. A Q&A will fo
 llow. David is a former PiA fellow whose path has taken him through inte
 rnational M&A law at Cravath\, advisory work at Goldman Sachs in London 
 and San Francisco\, and now his own Silicon Valley investment banking fi
 rm\, 52 Capital Partners. He also teaches finance at Santa Clara\, serve
 s on the Advisory Council of the Wythes Center on Contemporary China\, a
 nd is a member of the National Committee on U.S.-China Relations. He maj
 ored in East Asian Studies\, is fluent in Mandarin and played lacrosse a
 t Princeton. He enjoys speaking with students who are t\nRegister: https
 ://app.joinhandshake.com/edu/events/2049363\nhttps://careerdevelopment.p
 rinceton.edu/events/asia-wall-street-and-beyond-alums-global-career-path
URL:https://careerdevelopment.princeton.edu/events/asia-wall-street-and-b
 eyond-alums-global-career-path
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
