SUMMARY:The Other 2/3 of the Tree of Life: Invertebrate and Plant Fossils
 : 150 Years of Princeton Paleontology
DESCRIPTION:150 Years of Princeton Paleontology brings real fossils from 
 the University’s Geosciences collection\, alongside the publications d
 escribing them\, to tell the story of the scientific lineage that founde
 d modern vertebrate paleontology. Towering skeletons and fossilized bone
 s of bizarre\, long-extinct vertebrate animals have captivated humans fo
 r over two centuries\, but the science of paleontology first evolved out
  of studies of the other two thirds of the tree of life on Earth: plants
  and invertebrate animals. As foundational geological principles were be
 ing established in the 18th and 19th cent\nhttps://www.princeton.edu/eve
 nts/2026/other-23-tree-life-invertebrate-and-plant-fossils-150-years-pri
 nceton-paleontology
URL:https://www.princeton.edu/events/2026/other-23-tree-life-invertebrate
 -and-plant-fossils-150-years-princeton-paleontology
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
