SUMMARY:Right Here\, Right Now: Figuring Interpretation at the Sassetti C
 hapel\, Florence
DESCRIPTION:The Sassetti Chapel in Santa Trinita\, Florence was decorated
  by the Ghirlandaio workshop between 1483 and 1485. The main narrative s
 cenes show episodes from the life of St Francis\, but the representation
 s of these events include some strikingly contemporary elements. Among t
 hese are recognizable views of fifteenth-century Florence and numerous p
 ortraits of individuals who were still alive when the frescoes were made
 \, including the patron\, the artist and other identifiable individuals.
  In the first decade of the twentieth century Aby Warburg published two 
 foundational essays on the chapel\, in w\nhttps://www.princeton.edu/even
 ts/2026/right-here-right-now-figuring-interpretation-sassetti-chapel-flo
 rence
