SUMMARY:Haiku Open Forum
DESCRIPTION:Come write\, read and share haiku with the Princeton Haiku So
 ciety! Whether you've written hundreds or never tried one\, this open fo
 rum is a relaxed space to try the form\, hear others' work and talk abou
 t what makes a good haiku. We'll have a board for writing haiku together
  and copies of our anthology (Vol. 12 and 13). We'll also have free food
 \, including onigiri and seasonal Japanese treats. No experience needed\
 , just bring your curiosity. Funded by the GSG Events Board. This event 
 is open to all Princeton graduate students regardless of identity.\nhttp
