SUMMARY:The Constitution is Not Enough: Crucial Ingredients for Democracy
DESCRIPTION:Beneath growing perceptions of democratic fragility in the Un
 ited States (and elsewhere) lies a deeper problem: crucial preconditions
  for effective self-government are in short supply and the constitutiona
 l system itself is an obstacle to investments in four essential ingredie
 nts: education\, access to reliable news\, security against lethal viole
 nce\, and trust in the legal and economic systems sufficient to elicit c
 ooperation and fair play. Repeated efforts to secure a federal constitut
 ional right to education have failed in the courts. Legal\, technologica
 l\, and economic developments have destr\nhttps://www.princeton.edu/even
 ts/2026/constitution-not-enough-crucial-ingredients-democracy
