 ration between choreographers Rashaun Mitchell and Silas Riener\, Prince
 ton Class of 2006\, and pioneering filmmaker and video artist Charles At
 las. Mitchell\, Riener\, and Atlas are Merce Cunningham Dance Company al
 umni.The full project is an evening-length presentation in two parts: a 
 3D dance film featuring seven dancers and a live proscenium performance 
 with several dancers. The film offers speculative worlds and alternate p
 ossibilities in bold visual environments. The performance includes live-
 video capture with multiple cameras\, mi\nhttps://www.princeton.edu/even
 ts/2026/tesseract-3d
