SUMMARY:Responsible AI: From Images to Structured Data
DESCRIPTION:We'll cover turning scans and digitized materials into struct
 ured data using optical character recognition (OCR) and handwritten text
  recognition (HTR) tools\, then focus on evaluation: using the structure
  itself\, such as agreement across a row\, cross-checking a name against
  a tenure date\, to catch errors instead of trusting model output at fac
 e value. This session frames a shift that runs through the whole series:
  from writing code to reviewing and evaluating what a model produces. Pa
 rticipants will come away with a working OCR/HTR workflow for their own 
 image materials and a concrete set of e\nhttps://www.princeton.edu/event
