SUMMARY:Curator Talk | A Tale of Two Textiles: Exchange and Conflict in E
 ighteenth-Century South India
DESCRIPTION:Unraveling histories of design through eighteenth-century tex
 tiles from South Asia John Guy\, the Florence and Herbert Irving Curator
  of the Arts of South and Southeast Asia at the Metropolitan Museum of A
 rt\, will present on two extraordinary painted cotton cloths from south 
 India that demonstrate the dynamics of the international textile trade i
 n the first half of the eighteenth century. By reading their design hist
 ories and cultural memories\, Guy will show how these two pictorial clot
 hs offer a richer understanding of the complexities of textile design\, 
 commissioning\, production and consumpti\nhttps://www.princeton.edu/even
 ts/2026/curator-talk-tale-two-textiles-exchange-and-conflict-eighteenth-
