SUMMARY:The Cinderella of Cognitive Science: Why the Body Matters for Dec
 isions\, Models\, and AI
DESCRIPTION:Markus Raab Institute of Psychology\, GSU\, Cologne\, Germany
  Date: Tuesday\, November 17 Time: 11AM Location: PNI A30 How do we deci
 de what to do when the decision itself is a movement\, and there is bare
 ly time to think? The body remains a Cinderella of cognitive science: ce
 ntral to how people act in the world\, yet often peripheral to our expla
 nations of cognition. I argue that understanding naturalistic decisions 
 requires understanding the moving body and its interaction with the envi
 ronment. Drawing on experimental and modelling research\, I examine how 
 people use fast-and-frugal heuristics to c\nhttps://www.princeton.edu/ev
 ents/2026/cinderella-cognitive-science-why-body-matters-decisions-models
 -and-ai
URL:https://www.princeton.edu/events/2026/cinderella-cognitive-science-wh
 y-body-matters-decisions-models-and-ai
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
