SUMMARY:Verifying Code You Didn't Write: R Good Practices in the Age of A
 I
DESCRIPTION:This workshop is intended for anyone who works with code they
  did not write themselves: generated by AI assistants\, inherited from c
 ollaborators\, or adapted from online examples. No previous experience w
 ith AI tools is required. This session will cover the following topics: 
 checking your data and variable types before modeling\; sanity-checking 
 merges and sample sizes\; catching “silent errors” code that runs wi
 thout error but gives wrong results\, and simple habits for testing unfa
 miliar code\, etc. Examples use R\, but the principles apply to any stat
 istical software. Hardware/software prerequisi\nhttps://www.princeton.ed
 u/events/2026/verifying-code-you-didnt-write-r-good-practices-age-ai
URL:https://www.princeton.edu/events/2026/verifying-code-you-didnt-write-
 r-good-practices-age-ai
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
